nat44-ed: do not translate ICMP that VPP sends from a pool address

With the output feature, ED translated everything leaving an outside
interface, VPP's own packets included. A ping of the router's outside
address passed to ip4-local (ED lets ICMP to an interface address through
when there is no session), but the echo reply then went through
in2out-output with no session, got a new session and, with 0033, an
identifier folded into the worker's range: the peer dropped the reply. A
test router dropped most pings of its exits' addresses that way. ICMP
errors VPP raises from those addresses were translated the same way.

Leave ICMP whose source is a pool address untranslated, as patch 0025
does for NAT44-EI. Only ICMP: VPP's own TCP and UDP from a pool address
keep getting sessions, which their replies need to get back in, since ED
drops TCP and UDP to an interface address that has no session. Verified
on the test router with three exits (WAN, a bridged loopback and a
WireGuard tunnel): pings of each exit's address from its far side and
VPP's own pings out of each exit all answered.

--- a/src/plugins/nat/nat44-ed/nat44_ed_in2out.c
+++ b/src/plugins/nat/nat44-ed/nat44_ed_in2out.c
@@ -737,6 +737,17 @@
 }
 
 static_always_inline int
+nat44_ed_is_pool_address (snat_main_t *sm, ip4_address_t addr)
+{
+  snat_address_t *ap;
+
+  vec_foreach (ap, sm->addresses)
+    if (ap->addr.as_u32 == addr.as_u32)
+      return 1;
+  return 0;
+}
+
+static_always_inline int
 nat44_ed_not_translate_output_feature (snat_main_t *sm, vlib_buffer_t *b,
 				       ip4_header_t *ip, u16 src_port,
 				       u16 dst_port, u32 thread_index,
@@ -762,6 +773,15 @@
       return 1;
     }
 
+  /* Sent by VPP itself from a pool address, such as the reply to a ping of
+   * the router or an ICMP error it raises: no inside host has that source,
+   * so it needs no translation, which would give it a new identifier that
+   * the peer drops. Only ICMP: VPP's own TCP and UDP from a pool address
+   * get sessions, which their replies need to get back in. */
+  if (ip->protocol == IP_PROTOCOL_ICMP &&
+      nat44_ed_is_pool_address (sm, ip->src_address))
+    return 1;
+
   /* dst NAT check */
   if (is_multi_worker &&
       PREDICT_TRUE (!pool_is_free_index (
